@startuml Fluxo - Nextcloud AIO
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

title Fluxo — Nextcloud AIO (Nuvem + Talk + Office)
caption Setup inicial via mastercontainer e exposição via tailscale serve no host

skinparam actor {
  BorderColor #4A148C
  FontColor #4A148C
  BackgroundColor #F3E5F5
}

actor "Usuário" as user
participant "Navegador" as browser
participant "Host Linux" as nc_host
participant "Nextcloud AIO\nMastercontainer" as nc_master
participant "Nextcloud\nApache (:11000)" as nc_apache
participant "PostgreSQL 15\n(AIO gerenciado)" as nc_db
participant "coturn\n(TURN/STUN)" as coturn
participant "Collabora Online" as collabora

group Passo 1: Setup inicial (wizard, uma vez)
  user -> browser : "Acessa https://<IP>:8080\n(wizard setup inicial)"
  browser -> nc_master : "Configura domínio,\napps, backup"
  nc_master -> nc_master : "Baixa e gerencia\ncontainers internos"
  nc_master -> nc_apache : "Sobe Apache\nna porta 11000"
end

group Passo 2: Exposição via Tailscale (host-level)
  nc_host -> nc_host : "tailscale serve --bg\nhttp://127.0.0.1:11000"
end

group Passo 3: Acesso do dia a dia
  user -> browser : "Acessa https://nextcloud.<TAILNET>.ts.net"
  browser -> nc_host : "Host-level tailscale serve"
  nc_host -> nc_apache : "Proxy :11000"
end

group Passo 4: Upload de arquivos
  user -> nc_apache : "Upload de arquivos"
  nc_apache -> nc_db : "Metadados dos arquivos"
  nc_apache -> filesystem : "Salva em\n/mnt/ncdata/"
end

group Passo 5: Videochamada (Nextcloud Talk)
  user -> nc_apache : "Nextcloud Talk\n(videochamada)"
  nc_apache -> coturn : "TURN/STUN\n(se configurado)"
end

group Passo 6: Edição de documentos (Collabora)
  user -> nc_apache : "Editar documento\n(Collabora Online)"
  nc_apache -> collabora : "Proxy para\ncontainer Collabora"
end

note right
  **Diferença chave**: Nextcloud NÃO usa
  sidecar Tailscale. Usa tailscale serve
  direto no **host** (fora do container).
  AIO gerencia seus próprios containers
  (Talk, Collabora, DB, etc.).
end note

@enduml
